[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @program

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-001
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Ease of Integration
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Airframe, Propulsion, Actuation, Recovery
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Systems, Structures, Electrical
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Systems Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Pre-Launch
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-001.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The vehicle shall be fully integrated, launched, and recovered within 2 hours under nominal conditions.
RATIONALE: This requirement decomposes TVC-MO-004, specifically focusing on the vehicle, and giving a specific timeframe for complete turnaround. Most launch sites are open from 10 AM to 4 PM, so 2 hours is the absolute maximum each launch may take. This does not take into account failures, which are varied and more specifically specified in the Concept of Operations documents.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-002
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Flight Computer Fire Wire
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Recovery, Power
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Electrical
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Electrical Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Parachute Descent
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-002.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The on board rocket avionics shall have the ability to set off fire wire, with at least 3 channels available to fire.
RATIONALE: This derived requirement ensures the rocket avionics will be able to support redundant single-deploy recovery, along with an extra channel to support landing operations in the future, such as fire wire to release landing legs.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-003
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Flight Computer Data Logging
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Power, Flight_Software
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Electrical, Software
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Electrical Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-003.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The Flight Computer shall log all determined relevant flight data on an onboard SD-Card. This includes all raw sensor data (IMU, Barometer, other peripherals), relevant state estimation outputs (State Vector), actuator command outputs, individual control outputs, timestamps for each set of data, and current state of the state machine.
RATIONALE: This decomposes TVC-MO-005 to apply to flight computer onboard data logging, along with a more specific set of data to collect.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-004
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Relevant Telemetry Data
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Power, Flight_Software, Ground_Systems
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Electrical, Software
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Electrical Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-004.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The flight computer shall send relevant flight data to a ground station via telemetry data packets. This includes state estimation outputs (State Vector), actuator commands outputs, individual control outputs, timestamps since launch, and the current state of the state machine.
RATIONALE: This decomposes TVC-MO-005 to apply to telemetry to the ground station, along with more specific information on what to send.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-005
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Performance
TITLE: Gimbal Minimum Angle
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Actuation
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Structures Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Powered Ascent
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: Flight 1
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: TBD
RESOLUTION_OWNER: Controls Lead
RESOLUTION_PLAN: Controls subteam will use a completed GNCSim architecture, with an integrated model/simulation of the gimbal, in order to determine the minimum gimbal angle. The simulation shall prove that the minimum gimbal angle (along with other gimbal properties) provided allows the rocket to maintain attitude under environmental conditions. Simulation results must be produced before the gimbal CDR. If GNCSim is not finished/integrated in time to complete this task, off the shelf tools such as aeroVECTOR will be used in replacement.
RESOLUTION_DUE_DATE: October 16th
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-005,6,7.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The minimum actuation angle the gimbal shall be physically capable of is [TBD_GimAngle] degrees, in all directions (360 degrees).
RATIONALE: Based on results from GNCSim dynamic analysis, this will help establish the minimum ange the gimbal is capable of in order for the rocket to be physically capable of maintaining attitude, a fundamental function the rocket must have in order to meet system goals.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-001

