RESOLUTION_OWNER: Controls Lead
RESOLUTION_PLAN: Controls subteam will use a completed GNCSim architecture, with an integrated model/simulation of the gimbal, in order to determine the minimum gimbal velocity. The simulation shall prove that the minimum gimbal velocity (along with other gimbal properties) provided allows the rocket to maintain attitude under environmental conditions. Simulation results must be produced before the gimbal CDR. If GNCSim is not finished/integrated in time to complete this task, off the shelf tools such as aeroVECTOR will be used in replacement.
RESOLUTION_DUE_DATE: October 16th
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-005,6,7.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The minimum velocity the gimbal shall be physically capable of is [TBD_GimVel] degrees/sec.
RATIONALE: Based on results from GNCSim dynamic analysis, this will help establish the minimum speed the gimbal is capable of in order for the rocket to be physically capable of maintaining attitude, a fundamental function the rocket must have to meet system goals.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-007
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Performance
TITLE: Gimbal Minimum Actuation Fidelity
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Actuation
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Structures Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Powered Ascent
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: Flight 1
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: TBD
RESOLUTION_OWNER: Controls Lead
RESOLUTION_PLAN: Controls subteam will use a completed GNCSim architecture, with an integrated model/simulation of the gimbal, in order to determine the minimum gimbal fidelity. The simulation shall prove that the minimum gimbal fidelity (along with other gimbal properties) provided allows the rocket to maintain attitude under environmental conditions. Simulation results must be produced before the gimbal CDR. If GNCSim is not finished/integrated in time to complete this task, off the shelf tools such as aeroVECTOR will be used in replacement.
RESOLUTION_DUE_DATE: October 16th
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-005,6,7.md
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The minimum actuation fidelity the gimbal shall be physically capable of is [TBD_TVCFid] degrees. This means the gimbal shall be able to actuate to positions that are multiples of the actuation fidelity.
RATIONALE: Based on results from GNCSim dynamic analysis, this will help establish the minimum actuation fidelity the gimbal is capable of in order for the rocket to be physically capable of maintaining attitude, a fundamental function the rocket must have to meet system goals.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-008
LEVEL: L2
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Safety
TITLE: PCB Fire Wire Protection
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Electrical
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Electrical Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Pre-Launch
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-008.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The flight computer shall support a physical inhibit/enable switch for the fire wire, with physical on-board feedback of inhibit/enable status that the microcontroller can read.
RATIONALE: Inhibiting the fire wire switch is an important safety feature to ensure safe operations while handling the rocket up until launch operations. Feedback ensures the team is aware of the state of the fire wire.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-REQ-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-009
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Design Constraint
TITLE: PCB Test Points
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Electrical
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Electrical Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-009.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: For major board circuitry, such as the recovery circuit, it shall be possible to physically check voltage using test points on the board. Important power lines, recovery circuitry, microcontroller debugging, interfaces (CAN, JTAG), and more should include test points.
RATIONALE: This is both an important board design feature to allow for debugging in the case of failures during testing, and any last minute debugging required on the launch site.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-010
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Physical
TITLE: Flight Computer Accessibility
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Airframe
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Structures Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Pre-Launch
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-010.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: For important flight computer debugging interfaces, such as flashing code and MCU reset, these interfaces shall be accessible during all pre-launch activities until the rocket is placed on the launch rail/pad.
RATIONALE: This requirement ensures rapid debugging in the case of failures, and gives the option for quick fixes without major rocket de-integration.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-004

