[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-014
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Physical
TITLE: Max Dry Rocket Mass
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Airframe, Propulsion, Actuation, Avionics, Power, Recovery
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures, Electrical
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Systems Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-014.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The max dry mass of the rocket (mass without motors) shall be a maximum of 1050 grams.
RATIONALE: A simple, 1D simulation was put together in order to Validate this requirement. That simulation can be found in docs/Configuration/TVC-REQ-014 folder. This simple 1-D simulation is required, as OpenRocket cannot properly simulate the full flight of an unstable rocket. The mass of the rocket in the simulation was adjusted to find the absolute maximum mass that allowed for around 50 feet of altitude gain, with some tolerance. This ensures the rocket, assuming a mostly vertical flight, will not reach the ground before motor burnout.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MC-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-015
LEVEL: L2
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Physical
TITLE: Max Gimbal Mass
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Actuation
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Structures Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-015.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The max mass of all gimbal components shall be a maximum of 350 grams.
RATIONALE: Using previous program experience. From Scarlet (Gimbaled 2024-2025) the mass of the gimbal was ~200 grams, but increased to ~800 grams on HPRTVC. Seeing as the architecture of Gimbaled TVC (Being low powered) matches Scarlet, but has greater restrictions (Accuracy, Speed, etc..) the mass is taken from Scarlet, with increased margin to allow for improved design. Evidence used: Scarlet OpenRocket (https://gtvault.sharepoint.com/:u:/s/gnc/IQDRCPbbADz0RYDQvH_F3RmwAXq7m1veWlWSwlan1esaDzY?e=n7STTH), HPRTVC masses (https://gtvault.sharepoint.com/:x:/s/gnc/IQCGeS3jqrzLSpojEPm9eAjLARGwMWSQHF-htBPefCFhMYI?e=eN0qTY)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-REQ-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-016
LEVEL: L2
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Physical
TITLE: Max Avionics Mass
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Power
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Structures Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-016.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The max mass of all avionics components shall be a maximum of 450 grams.
RATIONALE: Using previous program experience. From Scarlet (Gimbaled 2024-2025) the mass of the avionics was ~500 grams, but increased to ~800 grams on HPRTVC. In order to accomodate other rocket changes, such as an improved gimbal, the mass budget for the avionics bay is slightly reduced. This is assumed to be practical, considering electrical team goals to make a lightweight, compact flight computer. Evidence used: Scarlet OpenRocket (https://gtvault.sharepoint.com/:u:/s/gnc/IQDRCPbbADz0RYDQvH_F3RmwAXq7m1veWlWSwlan1esaDzY?e=n7STTH), HPRTVC masses (https://gtvault.sharepoint.com/:x:/s/gnc/IQCGeS3jqrzLSpojEPm9eAjLARGwMWSQHF-htBPefCFhMYI?e=eN0qTY)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-REQ-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-017
LEVEL: L2
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Physical
TITLE: Max "other" mass
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Airframe, Recovery
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Structures
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Structures Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-017.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The max mass of all non-gimbal, non-avionics components shall be a maximum of 200 grams. 
RATIONALE: Considering TVC-REQ-014 and TVC-REQ-015, the remaining mass in order to meet TVC-REQ-014 is 250g. 200g is set as the requirement to allow for a margin in the rocket mass (5%, but other components also include a margin).Seeing as the remaining mass includes airframe, nosecone, and recovery, this is likely a reasonable constraint, especially considering previous program experience.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-REQ-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-018
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Specific Controls Shutoff Conditions
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Flight_Software
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Controls
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Controls Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: Powered Ascent
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: TBD
RESOLUTION_OWNER: Controls Lead
RESOLUTION_PLAN: Once a completed GNCSim architecture has been put together, and the Gimbaled TVC rocket is ready to simulate, a variety of unsafe conditions should be simulated via Monte Carlo (Rocket Angle from Vertical, Angular rates in Pitch, Yaw, and Roll). For each of these factors, a maximum safe condition shall be decided, based on whether the rocket can recover from the condition by the end of the burn of the motor. Because the values are a small change in software, this can be resolved later on in the design cycle. Additionally, GNCSim should simulate what happens after controls shutoff. GNCSim should consider cases of return back to 0, return back to 0 and cut power, just cutting power, etc...
RESOLUTION_DUE_DATE: December 1st
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-018.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The rocket controls shall be turned off when unsafe conditions are reached. Unsafe conditions include: (1) Rocket [TBD_UnsafeDeg] degrees from vertical, (2) Rocket has [TBD_UnsafeRate] angular rate in Pitch/Yaw, (3) Rocket has [TBD_UnsafeRate2] angular rate in Roll. Controls shutoff sequence requires: 1- Actuating the gimbal to the known 0 position 2- Cutting power from the gimbal actuators.
RATIONALE: This meets the parent requirement, ensuring that controls are shutoff once angle, or rates, are too high to recover from. At this point, it is assumed the controls are not working as expected, and likely are contributing to rocket unsafe conditions. 
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: TVC-REQ-019
LEVEL: L1
REQUIREMENT_TYPE: Design Constraint
TITLE: GNCSim for controls algorithm
APPLICABLE_SUBSYSTEM: Avionics, Flight_Software
SUBTEAM_OWNER: Controls
INDIVIDUAL_OWNER: Controls Lead
VEHICLE_CONFIGURATION: TVC-F1
MISSION_PHASE: All
FLIGHT_ATTEMPT: All
OPEN_ITEM_STATUS: None
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
VERIFICATION_PLAN_LINK: docs/verification/tvc-req-019.md
STATUS: Draft
STATEMENT: The controls team shall develop a full, closed-loop model of the Gimbaled TVC rocket in GNCSim in order find and tune the closed loop controls for the vehicle.
RATIONALE: In order to derive a control loop algorithm, the team must use GNCSim to model the rocket, the control algorithm, and use GNCSim to evaluate the control algorithm (Stability, Response Time, Steady State Error, etc...)
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: TVC-MO-009

